<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1. </span>Derived categories of sheaves on algebraic stacks</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we review derived categories of sheaves on algebraic
stacks. Fix an algebraic stack <math id="S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. We take <math id="S1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Mod}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Mod}({X})</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{QCoh}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{QCoh}({X})</annotation></semantics></math>) to
denote the abelian category of <math id="S1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules (resp. quasicoherent
<math id="S1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules) on the lisse-étale site of <math id="S1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx21" title="" class="ltx_ref">LMB</a>, 12.1]</cite>. Take <math id="S1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>) to denote
the unbounded derived category of <math id="S1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Mod}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Mod}({X})</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. the full
subcategory of <math id="S1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> with cohomology in <math id="S1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{QCoh}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{QCoh}({X})</annotation></semantics></math>). Superscripts
such as <math id="S1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq n</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> decorating <math id="S1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> should be interpreted as usual. In addition, if <math id="S1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is
locally noetherian, one may consider the category of coherent sheaves
<math id="S1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Coh}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Coh}({X})</annotation></semantics></math> and the derived category <math id="S1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>Coh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is a Deligne–Mumford stack, there is an
associated small étale site. We take <math id="S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Mod}({X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Mod}({X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}})</annotation></semantics></math>
(resp. <math id="S1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{QCoh}({X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{QCoh}({X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}})</annotation></semantics></math>) to denote the abelian category of
<math id="S1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules (resp. quasicoherent
<math id="S1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules). There are naturally induced morphisms of
abelian categories <math id="S1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Mod}({X})\to\mathbf{Mod}({X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Mod}({X})\to\mathbf{Mod}({X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{QCoh}({X})\to\mathbf{QCoh}({X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{QCoh}({X})\to\mathbf{QCoh}({X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Set <math id="S1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}})</annotation></semantics></math> to be the triangulated category
<math id="S1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathbf{QCoh}({X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}})}(\mathbf{Mod}({X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathbf{QCoh}({X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}})}(\mathbf{Mod}({X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}}))</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the natural functor
<math id="S1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)\to\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)\to\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}})</annotation></semantics></math> is an equivalence of
categories. If <math id="S1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is a scheme, the corresponding statement for the
Zariski site is also true.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For generalities on
unbounded derived categories on ringed sites, we refer the reader to
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx18" title="" class="ltx_ref">KS06</a>, §18.6]</cite>. We now record for future reference some useful
formulae. If <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>,
then there is the derived tensor product <math id="S1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes^{\mathsf{L}}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes^{\mathsf{L}}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, the derived sheaf
Hom functor <math id="S1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\in\mathsf{D}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\in\mathsf{D}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> and the
derived global Hom functor <math id="S1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}\!\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\in\mathsf{D}(\mathbf{Ab})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}\!\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\in\mathsf{D}(\mathbf{Ab})</annotation></semantics></math>. For all <math id="S1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{P}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{P}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> we have a functorial isomorphism:</p>
<table id="S1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes^{\mathsf{L}}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{P}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\cong\Hom_{\mathcal{O}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{P}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes^{\mathsf{L}}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{P}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\cong\Hom_{\mathcal{O}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{P}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">as well as a functorial quasi-isomorphism:</p>
<table id="S1.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes^{\mathsf{L}}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{P}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\simeq\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{P}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes^{\mathsf{L}}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{P}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\simeq\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{P}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Set <math id="S1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}\Gamma(X,-)=\mathsf{R}\!\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{O}_{X},-)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}\Gamma(X,-)=\mathsf{R}\!\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{O}_{X},-)</annotation></semantics></math>, then there
is also a natural quasi-isomorphism:</p>
<table id="S1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}\!\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\simeq\mathsf{R}\Gamma\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}\!\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\simeq\mathsf{R}\Gamma\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>,
then <math id="S1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes^{\mathsf{L}}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes^{\mathsf{L}}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. If
<math id="S1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is locally noetherian and <math id="S1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{-}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>Coh</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{-}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>,
then <math id="S1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes^{\mathsf{L}}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{-}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>Coh</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes^{\mathsf{L}}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{-}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, if <math id="S1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is locally noetherian and <math id="S1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}^{-}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}^{-}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{+}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>Coh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{+}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>), then
<math id="S1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>
(resp. <math id="S1.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{+}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>Coh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{+}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>). These results are all
consequences of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ols07</a>, §6]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx22" title="" class="ltx_ref">LO08</a>, §2]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a morphism of algebraic stacks <math id="S1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\to Y</annotation></semantics></math>. We let <math id="S1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}f_{*}:\mathsf{D}(X)\to\mathsf{D}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}f_{*}:\mathsf{D}(X)\to\mathsf{D}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the derived functor of <math id="S1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{*}:\mathbf{Mod}({X})\to\mathbf{Mod}({Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{*}:\mathbf{Mod}({X})\to\mathbf{Mod}({Y})</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, set:</p>
<table id="S1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}xt^{{q}}({f};{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}):=\mathcal{H}^{{q}}(\mathsf{R}f_{*}\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}xt^{{q}}({f};{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}):=\mathcal{H}^{{q}}(\mathsf{R}f_{*}\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">If the morphism <math id="S1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is quasicompact and quasiseparated,
then the restriction of <math id="S1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}f_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}f_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> induces a
functor <math id="S1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}:\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)\to\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}:\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)\to\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ols07</a>, Lem. 6.20]</cite>. If <math id="S1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> are Deligne–Mumford stacks, then
the restriction of <math id="S1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}f_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}f_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with the
restriction of the derived functor of <math id="S1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}})_{*}:\mathbf{Mod}({X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}})\to\mathbf{Mod}({Y_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}})_{*}:\mathbf{Mod}({X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}})\to\mathbf{Mod}({Y_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}})</annotation></semantics></math>. A consequence of
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx22" title="" class="ltx_ref">LO08</a>, Ex. 2.1.11]</cite> is that if in addition <math id="S1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is representable, then the
restriction of <math id="S1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}f_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}f_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S1.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> induces a functor <math id="S1.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}:\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)\to\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}:\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)\to\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">A morphism of algebraic stacks <math id="S1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\to Y</annotation></semantics></math>, however, does not
necessarily induce a left exact morphism of corresponding
lisse-étale sites <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Beh03</a>, 5.3.12]</cite>, thus the construction of
the correct derived functors of <math id="S1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}:\mathbf{QCoh}({Y})\to\mathbf{QCoh}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}:\mathbf{QCoh}({Y})\to\mathbf{QCoh}({X})</annotation></semantics></math> is
somewhat subtle. There are currently two approaches to constructing
these functors. The first, due to M. Olsson <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ols07</a>]</cite> and
Y. Laszlo and M. Olsson <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx22" title="" class="ltx_ref">LO08</a>]</cite>, uses cohomological
descent. The other approach appears in the Stacks Project
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Stacks</a>]</cite>. The latter approach is more widely applicable,
but uses a completely different formulation (big sites) and requires
significant amounts of technology that many people may not be familiar
with.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In this article, where there is always some finiteness at hand,
the approach of Olsson and Laszlo–Olsson is sufficient,
thus is the method that we will employ. In any case, there exists a
functor <math id="S1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}:\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(Y)\to\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}:\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(Y)\to\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{{0}}(\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{I}}[0])\cong f^{*}\mathcal{{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{{0}}(\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{I}}[0])\cong f^{*}\mathcal{{I}}</annotation></semantics></math>, whenever
<math id="S1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{I}}\in\mathbf{QCoh}({Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{I}}\in\mathbf{QCoh}({Y})</annotation></semantics></math>. In addition, if <math id="S1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is quasicompact and quasiseparated, <math id="S1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, then there is a
natural isomorphism:</p>
<table id="S1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{Y}}(\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\cong\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{Y}}(\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\cong\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="S1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the left adjoint of <math id="S1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}f_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}f_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the situation where <math id="S1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> are Deligne–Mumford stacks, there
also exists a derived functor <math id="S1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}f_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}^{*}:\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(Y_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}})\to\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}f_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}^{*}:\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(Y_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}})\to\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}})</annotation></semantics></math>. The restriction of <math id="S1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}f_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}f_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="S1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(Y_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>´</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(Y_{\mathrm{\acute{e}t}})</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with <math id="S1.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\to Y</annotation></semantics></math> is a quasicompact morphism of locally
noetherian algebraic stacks, <math id="S1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{-}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>Coh</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{-}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, the isomorphism (<a href="#S1.E4" title="In 1. Derived categories of sheaves on algebraic stacks ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a>) is
readily strengthened to a natural quasi-isomorphism
in <math id="S1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{Y}}(\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\simeq\mathsf{R}f_{*}\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{Y}}(\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\simeq\mathsf{R}f_{*}\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\to Y</annotation></semantics></math> is a representable and quasicompact morphism of
algebraic stacks, then the isomorphism
(<a href="#S1.E4" title="In 1. Derived categories of sheaves on algebraic stacks ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a>) can be extended to all <math id="S1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. In this situation—which is covered in
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx16" title="" class="ltx_ref">HR12c</a>]</cite>, generalizing
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nee96</a>, Prop. 5.3]</cite>—there is also the projection formula,
which gives a functorial quasi-isomorphism for all <math id="S1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="S1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\otimes^{\mathsf{L}}_{\mathcal{O}_{Y}}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\simeq\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}(\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes^{\mathsf{L}}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\otimes^{\mathsf{L}}_{\mathcal{O}_{Y}}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\simeq\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}(\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes^{\mathsf{L}}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">For a
morphism of algebraic stacks <math id="S1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\to Y</annotation></semantics></math> a complex <math id="S1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{-}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{-}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> has <em id="S1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">finite tor-dimension over <math id="S1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math></em> if there
exists a non-negative integer <math id="S1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="S1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{\geq i}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{\geq i}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> we have that <math id="S1.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{\geq i-n}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{\geq i-n}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. We conclude this section with
the following easily proven lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1.1</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix an affine noetherian scheme <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and a morphism of noetherian
algebraic stacks <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\to S</annotation></semantics></math>. Let
<math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{-}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>Coh</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{-}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{b}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>Coh</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{b}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math> has finite tor-dimension over <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>,
then the following functor preserves filtered colimits:</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}(-)):\mathbf{QCoh}({S})\to\mathbf{Ab}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝐀𝐛</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}(-)):\mathbf{QCoh}({S})\to\mathbf{Ab}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We now briefly review homotopy limits in a triangulated category
<math id="S1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> admitting countable products. Fix for each <math id="S1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> a
morphism in <math id="S1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}:T_{i+1}\to T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}:T_{i+1}\to T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Set <math id="S1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t:\Pi_{i\geq 0}T_{i}\to\Pi_{i\geq 0}T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t:\Pi_{i\geq 0}T_{i}\to\Pi_{i\geq 0}T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to be
the composition of the product of the morphisms <math id="S1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with the
projection <math id="S1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{i\geq 0}T_{i}\to\Pi_{i\geq 1}T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{i\geq 0}T_{i}\to\Pi_{i\geq 1}T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We define
<math id="S1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underset{i}{\mathrm{holim}}\,T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>holim</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑖</mo></munder><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underset{i}{\mathrm{holim}}\,T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> via the following distinguished triangle:</p>
<table id="S1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 2.5pt\hbox{\kern 22.75117pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;&amp;&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-22.75117pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\underset{i}{\mathrm{holim}}\,T_{i}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 46.75117pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 46.75117pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\prod_{i\geq 0}T_{i}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 103.81256pt\raise 5.43056pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.43056pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\mathrm{Id}-t}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 140.32301pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 110.32301pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 140.32301pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\prod_{i\geq 0}T_{i}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}\ignorespaces." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-21.447519123166597px" height="36.48" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="31.48 21.45 280.40 36.48" width="280.40"> <g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 31.480801060962797 36.47602229621774) translate(0,3.46) translate(31.48,0)"> <g transform="translate(-31.48,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.95em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.68" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="54.66"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>holim</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑖</mo></munder><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 31.480822174549434 -0.27673578005007266 L 31.480822174549434 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(64.69,0)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 31.480822174549434 -0.27673578005007266 L 64.6896013930508 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 64.6896013930508 -0.27673578005007266 L 64.6896013930508 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(64.69,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.36em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:1em;font-size:10pt;" height="23.29" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="46.45"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 119.44515470549891 -0.27673578005007266 L 119.44515470549891 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(143.65,0) translate(0,7.51) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.36)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.3em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.73" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="18.02"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">Id</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <g transform="translate(194.17,0)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 119.44515470549891 -0.27673578005007266 L 194.16495545269692 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 194.16495545269692 -0.27673578005007266 L 194.16495545269692 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(194.17,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.36em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:1em;font-size:10pt;" height="23.29" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="46.45"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> </g> </svg> </mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 2.5pt\hbox{\kern 22.75117pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;&amp;&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-22.75117pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\underset{i}{\mathrm{holim}}\,T_{i}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 46.75117pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 46.75117pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\prod_{i\geq 0}T_{i}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 103.81256pt\raise 5.43056pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.43056pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\mathrm{Id}-t}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 140.32301pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 110.32301pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 140.32301pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\prod_{i\geq 0}T_{i}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}\ignorespaces.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">The category of lisse-étale <math id="S1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules is a Grothendieck
abelian category, thus <math id="S1.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> admits small products. Moreover, we wish to
point out that the functors <math id="S1.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}\Gamma(X,-)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}\Gamma(X,-)</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S1.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },-)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },-)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S1.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S1.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}f_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}f_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for a morphism of algebraic stacks <math id="S1.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\to Y</annotation></semantics></math> all preserve
homotopy limits because they preserve products.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The following result is well-known and appears in
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Stacks</a>, <a target="_blank" href="http://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08IY" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">08IY</a>]</cite> (albeit in a slightly different,
but equivalent formulation).</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1.2</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be an algebraic stack and fix <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,
the projections <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\to\tau^{{\geq-i}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\to\tau^{{\geq-i}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math> induce a
non-canonical morphism:</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\to\underset{i}{\mathrm{holim}}\,\tau^{{\geq-i}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>holim</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑖</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\to\underset{i}{\mathrm{holim}}\,\tau^{{\geq-i}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, then any such <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is a quasi-isomorphism.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the main result of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nee11</a>]</cite>
produces—in positive characteristic—complexes <math id="S1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}(\mathbf{QCoh}({B\mathbb{N}_{a}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}(\mathbf{QCoh}({B\mathbb{N}_{a}}))</annotation></semantics></math> with the property that there are no quasi-isomorphisms:</p>
<table id="S1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\to\underset{i}{\mathrm{holim}}\,\tau^{{\geq-i}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>holim</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑖</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\to\underset{i}{\mathrm{holim}}\,\tau^{{\geq-i}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p11.2" class="ltx_p">We wish to emphasize that this does not contradict Lemma
<a href="#S1.Thmthm2" title="Lemma 1.2. ‣ 1. Derived categories of sheaves on algebraic stacks ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>. Indeed, while the categories
<math id="S1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}^{+}(\mathbf{QCoh}({B\mathbb{G}_{a}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝖣</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}^{+}(\mathbf{QCoh}({B\mathbb{G}_{a}}))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(B\mathbb{G}_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(B\mathbb{G}_{a})</annotation></semantics></math> are
equivalent <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lur04</a>, Thm. 3.8]</cite>, this equivalence does not
extend to the unbounded derived categories.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2. </span>Corepresentability of <math id="S2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om</annotation></semantics></math>-functors</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we prove Theorem <a href="#Thmmainthm2" title="Theorem B. ‣ Introduction ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>. Before
we get to this we require the
following two easily proven lemmas. Our first lemma gives two
important maps used to prove Theorem <a href="#Thmmainthm2" title="Theorem B. ‣ Introduction ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a morphism of noetherian algebraic stacks <math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\to S</annotation></semantics></math>. Let
<math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{-}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>Coh</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{-}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> have finite tor-dimension over <math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{F}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{-}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>Coh</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{F}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{-}(S)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{G}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{G}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(S)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="S2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is a natural morphism in </span><math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(S)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}(\mathcal{{{F}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{G}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\to\mathsf{R}f_{*}\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{F}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{G}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}(\mathcal{{{F}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{G}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\to\mathsf{R}f_{*}\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{F}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{G}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is a natural quasi-isomorphism in
</span><math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(X)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}(\mathcal{{{F}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{G}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\simeq\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{F}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{G}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}(\mathcal{{{F}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{G}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })\simeq\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{F}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{G}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our next lemma will give the compatibility of the corepresenting
object in Theorem <a href="#Thmmainthm2" title="Theorem B. ‣ Introduction ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> with base change—the
result for schemes boils down to the well-known tor-independent base
change <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx8" title="" class="ltx_ref">FGI+05</a>, Thm. 8.3.2]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.2</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a <math id="S2.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-cartesian square of noetherian algebraic stacks:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
