<tbody id="S2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\simeq\mathsf{R}f_{*}\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\simeq\mathsf{R}f_{*}\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.8.1" class="ltx_text">Note, however, that the maps above depend on <math id="S2.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="S2.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math> in a non-natural way (this is because <math id="S2.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underset{n}{\mathrm{holim}}\," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>holim</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑛</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underset{n}{\mathrm{holim}}\,</annotation></semantics></math> is
constructed as a cone, thus is not functorial). In any case,
corresponding to the identity map <math id="S2.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{E}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}\to\mathcal{{{E}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mtext>    </mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mtext>    </mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{E}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}\to\mathcal{{{E}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}</annotation></semantics></math> there is a morphism
<math id="S2.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}:\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\to\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{E}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mtext>    </mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}:\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\to\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{E}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}</annotation></semantics></math> (which is not necessarily
functorial in <math id="S2.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S2.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math>). Now take <math id="S2.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(S)</annotation></semantics></math>, then Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2. Corepresentability of 
        
          
            ⁢
            R
            H
            o
            m
          
        
      -functors ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>(<a href="#S2.I1.i1" title="item 1 ‣ Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2. Corepresentability of 
        
          
            ⁢
            R
            H
            o
            m
          
        
      -functors ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)
provides a natural sequence of maps:</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}(\mathcal{{{E}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mtext>    </mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}(\mathcal{{{E}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\to\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{E}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mtext>    </mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\to\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{E}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\to\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\to\mathsf{R}{f}_{*}\mathsf{R}\mathcal{H}om_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.9.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 2. Corepresentability of 
        
          
            ⁢
            R
            H
            o
            m
          
        
      -functors ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>), the map above is certainly a
quasi-isomorphism for all <math id="S2.p4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{+}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>Coh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{+}(S)</annotation></semantics></math>. To
show that it is a quasi-isomorphism for all
<math id="S2.p4.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{I}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{+}(S)</annotation></semantics></math>, by the “way-out right” results of
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Har66</a>, I.7.1]</cite>, it is sufficient to prove that it is a
quasi-isomorphism for all quasicoherent <math id="S2.p4.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules. We may now
reduce to the case where <math id="S2.p4.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is an affine and noetherian
scheme. Hence, it is sufficient to prove that the natural
transformation of functors from <math id="S2.p4.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{QCoh}({S})\to\mathbf{Ab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝐀𝐛</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{QCoh}({S})\to\mathbf{Ab}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}(\mathcal{{{E}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},(-)[0])\to\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}(-)[0])" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mtext>    </mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}(\mathcal{{{E}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},(-)[0])\to\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}(-)[0])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.10.1" class="ltx_text">is an isomorphism. By Lemma <a href="#S1.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 1.1. ‣ 1. Derived categories of sheaves on algebraic stacks ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>, both functors
preserve filtered colimits and the exhibited natural transformation
is an isomorphism for all <math id="S2.p4.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{I}}\in\mathbf{Coh}({S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{I}}\in\mathbf{Coh}({S})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since any <math id="S2.p4.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{I}}\in\mathbf{QCoh}({S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{I}}\in\mathbf{QCoh}({S})</annotation></semantics></math> is a filtered colimit of objects of <math id="S2.p4.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Coh}({S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Coh}({S})</annotation></semantics></math>, we
deduce the result.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">It now remains to address the compatibility of
<math id="S2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{E}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mtext>    </mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{E}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }_{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ },\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}</annotation></semantics></math> with base change in the situation
where <math id="S2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\simeq\mathcal{{N}}[0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\simeq\mathcal{{N}}[0]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{N}}\in\mathbf{Coh}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{N}}\in\mathbf{Coh}({X})</annotation></semantics></math> is
flat over <math id="S2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. So, we fix a morphism of noetherian algebraic stacks <math id="S2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:T\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:T\to S</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> admits a dualizing complex and form the
<math id="S2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-cartesian square of noetherian algebraic stacks:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
