<p id="S4.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">For all integers <math id="S4.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> we also have
isomorphisms</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{Q}}_{1}},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[r]}}\cong\prod_{\lambda}\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}_{\lambda}},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[r]}}\quad\mbox{and}\quad\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{Q}}_{2}},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[r]}}\cong\prod_{\lambda\leq\lambda^{\prime}}\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}_{\lambda}},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[r]}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mi>λ</mi></munder><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{Q}}_{1}},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[r]}}\cong\prod_{\lambda}\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}_{\lambda}},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[r]}}\quad\mbox{and}\quad\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{Q}}_{2}},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[r]}}\cong\prod_{\lambda\leq\lambda^{\prime}}\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}_{\lambda}},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[r]}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">By Examples <a href="#S3.Thmthm9" title="Example 3.9. ‣ 3. Finitely generated and coherent functors ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmthm5" title="Example 3.5. ‣ 3. Finitely generated and coherent functors ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>, together
with our hypotheses, we deduce that <math id="S4.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{{Q}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[r]}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{{Q}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[r]}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a
coherent functor for all <math id="S4.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, there is a distinguished
triangle <math id="S4.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{Q}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\to\mathcal{{M}}[-1]\to(\ker\theta)[1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{Q}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\to\mathcal{{M}}[-1]\to(\ker\theta)[1]</annotation></semantics></math>, thus we
obtain an exact sequence in <math id="S4.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Fun}_{{S}}^{\times}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐅𝐮𝐧</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>×</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Fun}_{{S}}^{\times}</annotation></semantics></math> for all integers <math id="S4.p8.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
