path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 43.60377912256123 -19.925229526644873 L 44.15725068266138 -19.925229526644873" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-8.79,0) translate(0,-30) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.67em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="9.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{S\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{S\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 8.792246428864846 -30.272217134692387 L 8.792246428864846 -29.71874557459224" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(14.92,0) translate(0,-22.82) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.14)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="5.75"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{g}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(31.98,0) translate(0,-30)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 8.792246428864846 -30.272217134692387 L 31.984550124533 -29.71874557459224" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 31.984550124533 -30.272217134692387 L 31.984550124533 -29.71874557459224" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(31.98,0) translate(0,-30) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.12em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="15.49"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{S_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{S_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> are affine schemes. Fix an integer <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and let
<math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{M}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{M}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{N}}_{0}\in\mathbf{QCoh}({X_{0}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{N}}_{0}\in\mathbf{QCoh}({X_{0}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume,
in addition, that <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{N}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{N}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is of finite presentation, flat
over <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and that the functors:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}_{0}},{\mathcal{{N}}_{0}[l]}}\quad\mbox{and}\quad\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{F}}},{(h^{*}\mathcal{{N}}_{0})[r]}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}_{0}},{\mathcal{{N}}_{0}[l]}}\quad\mbox{and}\quad\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{F}}},{(h^{*}\mathcal{{N}}_{0})[r]}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">are coherent for all integers <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> and for all integers <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;n</annotation></semantics></math> and all
<math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{F}}\in\mathbf{QCoh}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{F}}\in\mathbf{QCoh}({X})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the functors
<math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{{(h^{*}\mathcal{{M}}_{0})},{(h^{*}\mathcal{{N}}_{0})[r]}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{{(h^{*}\mathcal{{M}}_{0})},{(h^{*}\mathcal{{N}}_{0})[r]}}</annotation></semantics></math> are coherent for
all integers <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="S4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }:=\mathsf{L}{h}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{M}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }:=\mathsf{L}{h}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}\mathcal{{M}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{N}}:={h}^{*}\mathcal{{N}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{N}}:={h}^{*}\mathcal{{N}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given
integers <math id="S4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> set:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{r,l}:=\mathbb{H}_{{\tau^{{\geq-l}}\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{N}}[r+l]}}\quad\mbox{and}\quad W_{r,l}:=\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{H}^{{-l}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })},{\mathcal{{N}}[r]}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{r,l}:=\mathbb{H}_{{\tau^{{\geq-l}}\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{N}}[r+l]}}\quad\mbox{and}\quad W_{r,l}:=\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{H}^{{-l}}(\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ })},{\mathcal{{N}}[r]}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">It is sufficient to prove that <math id="S4.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{r,l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{r,l}</annotation></semantics></math> is coherent for all
<math id="S4.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq n</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="S4.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> (the result follows by taking <math id="S4.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=0</annotation></semantics></math>). Now, for
integers <math id="S4.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> we have a distinguished triangle in
<math id="S4.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
