</table>
<p id="S4.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">Applying to this triangle the functor
<math id="S4.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(-,\mathcal{{N}}[r+l]\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}(-))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(-,\mathcal{{N}}[r+l]\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}(-))</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain an exact sequence in <math id="S4.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Fun}_{{S}}^{\times}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐅𝐮𝐧</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>×</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Fun}_{{S}}^{\times}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.E1.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="21.72" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-11.569253138458645px" version="1.1" viewBox="27.76 11.57 398.11 21.72" width="398.11"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 27.758961349366956 21.716358421814462) translate(0,3.46) translate(27.76,0)"><g transform="translate(-27.76,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.41em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="47.22"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.E1.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{V_{r-2,l+1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{V_{r-2,l+1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 27.758961349366956 -0.27673578005007266 L 27.758961349366956 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(60.97,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 27.758961349366956 -0.27673578005007266 L 60.96776168145496 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 60.96776168145496 -0.27673578005007266 L 60.96776168145496 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(60.97,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.69em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="51.06"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.E1.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{W_{r-2,l+1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{W_{r-2,l+1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 120.32930725950645 -0.27673578005007266 L 120.32930725950645 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(153.54,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 120.32930725950645 -0.27673578005007266 L 153.5380864780078 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 153.5380864780078 -0.27673578005007266 L 153.5380864780078 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(153.54,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.69em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="23.37"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.E1.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{V_{r,l}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{V_{r,l}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 185.2062917339599 -0.27673578005007266 L 185.2062917339599 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(218.42,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 185.2062917339599 -0.27673578005007266 L 218.41507095246126 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 218.41507095246126 -0.27673578005007266 L 218.41507095246126 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(218.42,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.41em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="47.22"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.E1.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{V_{r-1,l+1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{V_{r-1,l+1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 273.93299365119515 -0.27673578005007266 L 273.93299365119515 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(307.15,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 273.93299365119515 -0.27673578005007266 L 307.14179398328315 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 307.14179398328315 -0.27673578005007266 L 307.14179398328315 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(307.15,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.97em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="54.9"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.E1.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{W_{r-1,l+1}.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{W_{r-1,l+1}.}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">By hypothesis, <math id="S4.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{r,l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{r,l}</annotation></semantics></math> is coherent for all <math id="S4.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> and all
<math id="S4.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;n</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, by Example <a href="#S3.Thmthm5" title="Example 3.5. ‣ 3. Finitely generated and coherent functors ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>, the result will follow
from the assertion that <math id="S4.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{r,l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{r,l}</annotation></semantics></math> is coherent for all <math id="S4.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> and all
<math id="S4.p10.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;n</annotation></semantics></math>. By induction on <math id="S4.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, the exact sequence
(<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Proof. ‣ 4. Coherence of 
        
          Hom
        
      -functors: flat case ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>) shows that it is sufficient to prove that
<math id="S4.p10.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{r,l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{r,l}</annotation></semantics></math> is coherent for all integers <math id="S4.p10.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="S4.p10.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{N}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{N}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-flat, the natural transformation of
functors <math id="S4.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{{\tau^{{\geq 0}}\mathcal{{{L}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{N}}}}\to\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{{L}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{N}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{{\tau^{{\geq 0}}\mathcal{{{L}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{N}}}}\to\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{{L}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{N}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism for all <math id="S4.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{L}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{L}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, if <math id="S4.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{r,l}=\mathbb{H}_{{\tau^{{\geq-l}}\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{N}}[r+l]}}\cong\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{N}}[r+l]}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{r,l}=\mathbb{H}_{{\tau^{{\geq-l}}\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{N}}[r+l]}}\cong\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{N}}[r+l]}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, if <math id="S4.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{{\geq-l}}\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\simeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><mo>≃</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{{\geq-l}}\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\simeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S4.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{r,l}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{r,l}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, it remains
to show that <math id="S4.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{N}}[l]}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{N}}[l]}}</annotation></semantics></math> is coherent for all
<math id="S4.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\in\mathbf{QCoh}({S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\in\mathbf{QCoh}({S})</annotation></semantics></math>,
then Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm2" title="Lemma 2.2. ‣ 2. Corepresentability of 
        
          
            ⁢
            R
            H
            o
            m
          
        
      -functors ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> gives a natural isomorphism
<math id="S4.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{N}}[l]}}(I)\cong\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}_{0}},{\mathcal{{N}}_{0}[l]}}(g_{*}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }},{\mathcal{{N}}[l]}}(I)\cong\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}_{0}},{\mathcal{{N}}_{0}[l]}}(g_{*}I)</annotation></semantics></math>. Example <a href="#S3.Thmthm6" title="Example 3.6. ‣ 3. Finitely generated and coherent functors ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a> now
gives the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p12.1" class="ltx_p">We can now prove Theorem
<a href="#Thmmainthm3" title="Theorem C. ‣ Introduction ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem
<a href="#Thmmainthm3" title="Theorem C. ‣ Introduction ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">We must prove that
<math id="S4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)=\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathcal{{N}}[0]}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)=\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathcal{{N}}[0]}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4. Coherence of 
        
          Hom
        
      -functors: flat case ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>,
we may immediately reduce to the case where <math id="S4.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\to S</annotation></semantics></math> is proper and of
finite presentation. Next, by Lemma
<a href="#S4.Thmthm2" title="Lemma 4.2. ‣ 4. Coherence of 
        
          Hom
        
      -functors: flat case ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>(<a href="#S4.I1.i2" title="item 2 ‣ Lemma 4.2. ‣ 4. Coherence of 
        
          Hom
        
      -functors: flat case ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), it
suffices to prove that <math id="S4.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}},{\mathcal{{N}}[n]}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}},{\mathcal{{N}}[n]}}</annotation></semantics></math> is coherent
for all integers <math id="S4.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, and all quasicoherent <math id="S4.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules
<math id="S4.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, <math id="S4.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}},{\mathcal{{N}}[n]}}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}},{\mathcal{{N}}[n]}}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and all
<math id="S4.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{M}}\in\mathbf{QCoh}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{M}}\in\mathbf{QCoh}({X})</annotation></semantics></math>. We now prove, by induction on <math id="S4.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq-1</annotation></semantics></math>,
that <math id="S4.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}},{\mathcal{{N}}[n]}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}},{\mathcal{{N}}[n]}}</annotation></semantics></math> is coherent. Certainly, the result
is true for <math id="S4.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we fix <math id="S4.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and assume the result
has been proven for all <math id="S4.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm4" title="Lemma 4.4. ‣ 4. Coherence of 
        
          Hom
        
      -functors: flat case ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>, it suffices to prove that
<math id="S4.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}},{\mathcal{{N}}[n]}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}},{\mathcal{{N}}[n]}}</annotation></semantics></math> is coherent when <math id="S4.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> is of finite
presentation. Thus, by standard limit methods
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ryd09</a>, Prop. B.3]</cite>, there exists an affine scheme <math id="S4.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> of
finite type over <math id="S4.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\spec\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\spec\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, a proper morphism of algebraic stacks
<math id="S4.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{0}:X_{0}\to S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{0}:X_{0}\to S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a morphism of affine schemes <math id="S4.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:S\to S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:S\to S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> inducing an isomorphism of algebraic stacks <math id="S4.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:X\to X_{0}\times_{S_{0}}S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:X\to X_{0}\times_{S_{0}}S</annotation></semantics></math>. This data may be chosen so that there exists
coherent <math id="S4.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{X_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{X_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules <math id="S4.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{M}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{M}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{N}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{N}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, with
<math id="S4.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{N}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{N}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> flat over <math id="S4.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, as well as isomorphisms of
<math id="S4.p15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules <math id="S4.p15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{*}\mathcal{{N}}_{0}\cong\mathcal{{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{*}\mathcal{{N}}_{0}\cong\mathcal{{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{*}\mathcal{{M}}_{0}\cong\mathcal{{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{*}\mathcal{{M}}_{0}\cong\mathcal{{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Theorem <a href="#Thmmainthm2" title="Theorem B. ‣ Introduction ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> and Example
<a href="#S3.Thmthm13" title="Example 3.13. ‣ 3. Finitely generated and coherent functors ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.13</span></a> the functors <math id="S4.p15.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}_{0}},{\mathcal{{N}}_{0}[l]}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{M}}_{0}},{\mathcal{{N}}_{0}[l]}}</annotation></semantics></math>
are coherent for all <math id="S4.p15.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm5" title="Lemma 4.5. ‣ 4. Coherence of 
        
          Hom
        
      -functors: flat case ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a> and the
inductive hypothesis, the result follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>Coherence of <math id="S5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Hom" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Hom</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Hom</annotation></semantics></math>-functors: non-flat case</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we prove Theorem
<a href="#Thmmainthm5" title="Theorem E. ‣ Introduction ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>. For this section we also retain the notation of
§<a href="#S4" title="4. Coherence of 
        
          Hom
        
      -functors: flat case ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. We begin by dispatching Theorem
<a href="#Thmmainthm5" title="Theorem E. ‣ Introduction ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> in the projective case.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix an affine and noetherian scheme <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, a morphism of schemes <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\to S</annotation></semantics></math> which is projective, and <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{b}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>Coh</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{b}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm2" title="Lemma 4.2. ‣ 4. Coherence of 
        
          Hom
        
      -functors: flat case ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>(<a href="#S4.I1.i1" title="item 1 ‣ Lemma 4.2. ‣ 4. Coherence of 
        
          Hom
        
      -functors: flat case ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), it is sufficient to show that
<math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{-}(X)\subseteq\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{-}(X)\subseteq\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is a
projective morphism and <math id="S5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is an affine and noetherian scheme, <math id="S5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>
has an ample family of line bundles. It now follows from
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx32" title="" class="ltx_ref">SGA6</a>, II.2.2.9]</cite> that if <math id="S5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{-}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}^{-}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="S5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{M}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math> is quasi-isomorphic to a complex <math id="S5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{Q}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{Q}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math> whose terms
are direct sums of shifts of line bundles. Thus, by Lemma
<a href="#S4.Thmthm2" title="Lemma 4.2. ‣ 4. Coherence of 
        
          Hom
        
      -functors: flat case ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, it is sufficient to prove that if
<math id="S5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{L}}\in\mathbf{Coh}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{L}}\in\mathbf{Coh}({X})</annotation></semantics></math> is a line bundle, then <math id="S5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{L}}[0]\in\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{L}}[0]\in\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix <math id="S5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have
natural isomorphisms:</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{L}}[0]},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[n]}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{L}}[0]},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[n]}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{L}}[0],\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[n]\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}(-))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{L}}[0],\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[n]\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}(-))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\cong\mathcal{H}^{{0}}(\mathsf{R}\Gamma(X,(\mathcal{{L}}^{-1}[0]\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[n]\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}(-))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mi>𝖫</mi><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cong\mathcal{H}^{{0}}(\mathsf{R}\Gamma(X,(\mathcal{{L}}^{-1}[0]\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[n]\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathsf{L}{f}_{\mathrm{Q}}^{*}(-))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cong\mathcal{H}^{{0}}(\mathsf{R}\Gamma(X,\mathcal{{L}}^{-1}[0]\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[n])\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}^{\mathsf{L}}(-))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cong\mathcal{H}^{{0}}(\mathsf{R}\Gamma(X,\mathcal{{L}}^{-1}[0]\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[n])\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}^{\mathsf{L}}(-)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">the latter isomorphism is given by the projection formula
(<a href="#S1.E6" title="In 1. Derived categories of sheaves on algebraic stacks ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.6</span></a>). Since <math id="S5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>-flat and
<math id="S5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{b}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>Coh</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{b}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that
<math id="S5.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{L}}^{-1}[0]\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[n]\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{b}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>Coh</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{L}}^{-1}[0]\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[n]\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{b}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="S5.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}\Gamma(X,\mathcal{{L}}^{-1}[0]\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[n])\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{b}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mi>𝖫</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>Coh</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}\Gamma(X,\mathcal{{L}}^{-1}[0]\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}^{\mathsf{L}}\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[n])\in\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{Coh}}^{b}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx32" title="" class="ltx_ref">SGA6</a>, III.2.2]</cite>. By Example
<a href="#S3.Thmthm13" title="Example 3.13. ‣ 3. Finitely generated and coherent functors ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.13</span></a>, <math id="S5.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{L}}},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[n]}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}_{{\mathcal{{L}}},{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }[n]}}</annotation></semantics></math> is
coherent, so <math id="S5.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{L}}[0]\in\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{L}}[0]\in\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We can now prove Theorem
<a href="#Thmmainthm5" title="Theorem E. ‣ Introduction ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem
<a href="#Thmmainthm5" title="Theorem E. ‣ Introduction ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By inducting on the length of the complex <math id="S5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math>, it is
sufficient to prove the result when <math id="S5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math> is only
supported in cohomological degree <math id="S5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, there exists a
closed immersion <math id="S5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i:Y\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i:Y\to X</annotation></semantics></math>, such that the composition <math id="S5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\circ i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\circ i</annotation></semantics></math> is proper, together with a coherent <math id="S5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>-module
<math id="S5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{N}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{N}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and a quasi-isomorphism <math id="S5.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{*}\mathcal{{N}}_{0}[0]\cong\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{*}\mathcal{{N}}_{0}[0]\cong\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4. Coherence of 
        
          Hom
        
      -functors: flat case ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, it suffices to
prove that <math id="S5.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{{Y/S}}^{{\mathcal{{N}}_{0}[0]}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{{Y/S}}^{{\mathcal{{N}}_{0}[0]}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, we have reduced the claim to the
case where the morphism <math id="S5.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is proper and where <math id="S5.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\simeq\mathcal{{N}}[0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>    </mtext></msup><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{{N}}}^{\,\begin{picture}(0.0,-2.0)\circle*{1.5}\end{picture}\ }\simeq\mathcal{{N}}[0]</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S5.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{N}}\in\mathbf{Coh}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{N}}\in\mathbf{Coh}({X})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now let <math id="S5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}\subset\mathbf{Coh}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}\subset\mathbf{Coh}({X})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the full subcategory
with objects those <math id="S5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{N}}\in\mathbf{Coh}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{N}}\in\mathbf{Coh}({X})</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathcal{{N}}[0]}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathcal{{N}}[0]}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. By the 5-Lemma,
it is plain to see that <math id="S5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an exact subcategory (in the
sense of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx6" title="" class="ltx_ref">EGA</a>, III.3.1]</cite>). We now prove by
noetherian induction on the closed substacks of <math id="S5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> that <math id="S5.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}=\mathbf{Coh}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}=\mathbf{Coh}({X})</annotation></semantics></math>. By virtue of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4. Coherence of 
        
          Hom
        
      -functors: flat case ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> and the
technique of dévissage <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx6" title="" class="ltx_ref">EGA</a>, Proof of III.3.2]</cite>, it is sufficient to
prove that <math id="S5.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}=\mathbf{Coh}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}=\mathbf{Coh}({X})</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S5.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is integral and
<math id="S5.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathcal{{Q}}[0]}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathcal{{Q}}[0]}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> for all coherent
<math id="S5.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules <math id="S5.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S5.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\supp\mathcal{{Q}}\subsetneq|X|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow><mo>⊊</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\supp\mathcal{{Q}}\subsetneq|X|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">So, we fix <math id="S5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{N}}\in\mathbf{Coh}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{N}}\in\mathbf{Coh}({X})</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining Chow’s Lemma
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx6" title="" class="ltx_ref">EGA</a>, II.5.6.1]</cite> with <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx7" title="" class="ltx_ref">EHKV01</a>, Thm. 2.7]</cite>,
there exists a morphism <math id="S5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p:X^{\prime}\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p:X^{\prime}\to X</annotation></semantics></math> that is proper, surjective, and
generically finite such that <math id="S5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a projective
<math id="S5.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>-scheme. The diagonal of <math id="S5.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, thus <math id="S5.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime\prime}:=X^{\prime}\times_{X}X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime\prime}:=X^{\prime}\times_{X}X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is
also a projective <math id="S5.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>-scheme, denote by <math id="S5.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q:X^{\prime\prime}\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q:X^{\prime\prime}\to X</annotation></semantics></math> the induced morphism. By Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm1" title="Lemma 5.1. ‣ 5. Coherence of 
        
          Hom
        
      -functors: non-flat case ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>
we deduce that <math id="S5.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{{X^{\prime}/S}}^{{p^{*}\mathcal{{N}}[0]}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{{X^{\prime}/S}}^{{p^{*}\mathcal{{N}}[0]}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{{X^{\prime\prime}/S}}^{{q^{*}\mathcal{{N}}[0]}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{{X^{\prime\prime}/S}}^{{q^{*}\mathcal{{N}}[0]}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, by Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4. Coherence of 
        
          Hom
        
      -functors: flat case ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, <math id="S5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathsf{R}p_{*}p^{*}\mathcal{{N}}}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\mathsf{R}p_{*}p^{*}\mathcal{{N}}}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, <math id="S5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is generically finite, thus
generically affine, so the support of the cohomology sheaves of
<math id="S5.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{{\geq 1}}(\mathsf{R}p_{*}p^{*}\mathcal{{N}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{{\geq 1}}(\mathsf{R}p_{*}p^{*}\mathcal{{N}})</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes generically. In
particular, by noetherian induction, we deduce that
<math id="S5.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\tau^{{\geq 1}}(\mathsf{R}p_{*}p^{*}\mathcal{{N}})}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{\tau^{{\geq 1}}(\mathsf{R}p_{*}p^{*}\mathcal{{N}})}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, thus
<math id="S5.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{p_{*}p^{*}\mathcal{{N}}[0]}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{p_{*}p^{*}\mathcal{{N}}[0]}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. An identical analysis
for <math id="S5.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> also proves that <math id="S5.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{q_{*}q^{*}\mathcal{{N}}[0]}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>QCoh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{{X/S}}^{{q_{*}q^{*}\mathcal{{N}}[0]}}=\mathsf{D}_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>
and so <math id="S5.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{*}p^{*}\mathcal{{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{*}p^{*}\mathcal{{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{*}q^{*}\mathcal{{N}}\in\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{*}q^{*}\mathcal{{N}}\in\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,
the equalizer <math id="S5.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{{N}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{{N}}}</annotation></semantics></math> of the two maps <math id="S5.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{*}p^{*}\mathcal{{N}}\rightrightarrows q_{*}q^{*}\mathcal{{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇉</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{*}p^{*}\mathcal{{N}}\rightrightarrows q_{*}q^{*}\mathcal{{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to <math id="S5.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Of course,
there is also a natural map <math id="S5.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta:\mathcal{{N}}\to\tilde{\mathcal{{N}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta:\mathcal{{N}}\to\tilde{\mathcal{{N}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. But
<math id="S5.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is integral, thus there is a dense open <math id="S5.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subset X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subset X</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S5.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{-1}(U)\to U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{-1}(U)\to U</annotation></semantics></math> is flat. By flat descent, <math id="S5.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is
an isomorphism over <math id="S5.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. So the exactness of the subcategory
<math id="S5.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}\subset\mathbf{Coh}({X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}\subset\mathbf{Coh}({X})</annotation></semantics></math> and dévissage now prove that
<math id="S5.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{N}}\in\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{N}}\in\mathcal{C}_{{X/S}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6. </span>Applications</h2>

<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1. </span>Representability of <math id="S6.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Hom" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Hom</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Hom</annotation></semantics></math>-spaces</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As promised, Theorem <a href="#Thmmainthm4" title="Theorem D. ‣ Introduction ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a> is now completely
elementary.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmmainthm4" title="Theorem D. ‣ Introduction ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The latter claim follows from the former by standard limit methods.
Now, <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\Hom}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}/S}(\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>Hom</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\Hom}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}/S}(\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}})</annotation></semantics></math> is an étale sheaf,
thus it is sufficient to prove the result in the case where <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is
affine. By Theorem <a href="#Thmmainthm3" title="Theorem C. ‣ Introduction ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>, the functor:</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}}\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}{f}^{*}(-)):\mathbf{QCoh}({S})\to\mathbf{Ab}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝐀𝐛</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}}\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}{f}^{*}(-)):\mathbf{QCoh}({S})\to\mathbf{Ab}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">is coherent. The flatness of
<math id="S6.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> also shows that this functor is left-exact, so by
Example <a href="#S3.Thmthm10" title="Example 3.10. ‣ 3. Finitely generated and coherent functors ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a>, it is corepresentable by a
quasicoherent <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. So, fixing an
affine <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>-scheme <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T\xrightarrow{\tau}S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝜏</mo></mover><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T\xrightarrow{\tau}S)</annotation></semantics></math>, there are natural
isomorphisms:</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\underline{\Hom}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}/S}(\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}})[T\xrightarrow{\tau}S]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>Hom</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝜏</mo></mover><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underline{\Hom}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}/S}(\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}})[T\xrightarrow{\tau}S]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X_{T}}}(\tau_{X}^{*}\mathcal{{M}},\tau_{X}^{*}\mathcal{{N}})\cong\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{M}},(\tau_{X})_{*}\tau_{X}^{*}\mathcal{{N}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X_{T}}}(\tau_{X}^{*}\mathcal{{M}},\tau_{X}^{*}\mathcal{{N}})\cong\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{M}},(\tau_{X})_{*}\tau_{X}^{*}\mathcal{{N}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cong\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}}\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}{f}^{*}[\tau_{*}\mathcal{O}_{T}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cong\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}(\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}}\otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X}}{f}^{*}[\tau_{*}\mathcal{O}_{T}])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cong\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}(Q_{\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}}},\tau_{*}\mathcal{O}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cong\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}(Q_{\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}}},\tau_{*}\mathcal{O}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cong\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{S}\text{-}\mathrm{Alg}}(\mathrm{Sym}^{\bullet}_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}Q_{\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}}},\tau_{*}\mathcal{O}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Hom</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Alg</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Sym</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>∙</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cong\Hom_{\mathcal{O}_{S}\text{-}\mathrm{Alg}}(\mathrm{Sym}^{\bullet}_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}Q_{\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}}},\tau_{*}\mathcal{O}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\cong\Hom_{\mathbf{Sch}/{S}}(T\xrightarrow{\tau}S,\underline{\spec}_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}\mathrm{Sym}^{\bullet}_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}Q_{\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>Hom</mi><mrow><mi>𝐒𝐜𝐡</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝜏</mo></mover><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>Spec</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></msub><msubsup><mi>Sym</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>∙</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cong\Hom_{\mathbf{Sch}/{S}}(T\xrightarrow{\tau}S,\underline{\spec}_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}\mathrm{Sym}^{\bullet}_{\mathcal{O}_{S}}Q_{\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">The natural isomorphism above extends to all <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>-schemes as
<math id="S6.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\Hom}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}/S}(\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>Hom</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\Hom}_{\mathcal{O}_{X}/S}(\mathcal{{M}},\mathcal{{N}})</annotation></semantics></math> is an étale sheaf. The
result follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2. </span>Cohomology and base change</h3>

<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To prove Theorem <a href="#Thmmainthm1" title="Theorem A. ‣ Introduction ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, we will consider some
refinements of the vanishing results of A. Ogus and G. Bergman
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx27" title="" class="ltx_ref">OB72</a>]</cite> that occur in the setting of finitely generated
functors. So, we fix a ring <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and an <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-linear functor <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({A})</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</p>
<table id="S6.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{V}(Q)=\{\mathfrak{p}\in\spec A\,:\,Q(N)=0\quad\forall N\in\mathbf{Mod}({A_{\mathfrak{p}}})\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝔭</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Spec</mi><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.448em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}(Q)=\{\mathfrak{p}\in\spec A\,:\,Q(N)=0\quad\forall N\in\mathbf{Mod}({A_{\mathfrak{p}}})\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Finitely generated functors immediately demonstrate their utility.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 6.1</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a ring <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and an <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-linear functor <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({A})</annotation></semantics></math> which preserves direct limits. If the functor <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is
finitely generated, then the set <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}(F)\subset\spec A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}(F)\subset\spec A</annotation></semantics></math> is Zariski open.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix a generator <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I,\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I,\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> and a prime ideal <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{p}\triangleleft A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔭</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊲</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{p}\triangleleft A</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{A_{\mathfrak{p}}}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{A_{\mathfrak{p}}}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math>
there is the localisation morphism <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{a}:I\to I_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{a}:I\to I_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>
(resp. <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{\mathfrak{p}}:I\to I_{\mathfrak{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{\mathfrak{p}}:I\to I_{\mathfrak{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>) and we set <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{a}=(l_{a})_{*}\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{a}=(l_{a})_{*}\eta</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\mathfrak{p}}=(l_{\mathfrak{p}})_{*}\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\mathfrak{p}}=(l_{\mathfrak{p}})_{*}\eta</annotation></semantics></math>). Since <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(I_{\mathfrak{p}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(I_{\mathfrak{p}})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, it
follows that
<math id="S6.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\mathfrak{p}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\mathfrak{p}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. However, as <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathfrak{p}}=\varinjlim_{a\notin\mathfrak{p}}I_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>lim</mi><mo>→</mo></munder><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>𝔭</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathfrak{p}}=\varinjlim_{a\notin\mathfrak{p}}I_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> and the functor <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> commutes
with direct limits of <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-modules, there exists <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\notin\mathfrak{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>𝔭</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\notin\mathfrak{p}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{a}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{a}=0</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(I_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(I_{a})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the pair
<math id="S6.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I_{a},\eta_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I_{a},\eta_{a})</annotation></semantics></math> generates <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{A_{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{A_{a}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{A_{a}}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{A_{a}}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We now record for future reference a result that is likely well-known,
though we are unaware of a reference. For an <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, define
<math id="S6.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{N}:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Sets}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝐒𝐞𝐭𝐬</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{N}:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Sets}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the
functor <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q(-\otimes_{A}N):\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Sets}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝐒𝐞𝐭𝐬</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(-\otimes_{A}N):\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Sets}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For another ring <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, a <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, and a functor <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({C})</annotation></semantics></math>, there is the functor <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\otimes_{C}K:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({C}):M\mapsto G(M)\otimes_{C}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>C</mi></msub><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>C</mi></msub><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\otimes_{C}K:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({C}):M\mapsto G(M)\otimes_{C}K</annotation></semantics></math>. Given an
<math id="S6.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-linear functor <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({A})</annotation></semantics></math>, and any <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S6.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>,
there is a natural transformation of functors</p>
<table id="S6.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{H,N}:H\otimes_{A}N\Rightarrow H^{N}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{H,N}:H\otimes_{A}N\Rightarrow H^{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 6.2</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a ring <math id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, and an <math id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-linear functor <math id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({A})</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that the functor <math id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> preserves direct
limits. Then, for any flat <math id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, the natural
transformation</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{F,M}:F\otimes_{A}M\Rightarrow F^{M}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{F,M}:F\otimes_{A}M\Rightarrow F^{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is an isomorphism of functors.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, assume that the <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is finite free. The functor
<math id="S6.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> commutes with finite products, thus the natural transformation
<math id="S6.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{F,M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{F,M}</annotation></semantics></math> induces an isomorphism. For the general case, by
Lazard’s Theorem
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Laz64</a>]</cite>, we may write <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\varinjlim_{i}P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>lim</mi><mo>→</mo></munder><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\varinjlim_{i}P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each
<math id="S6.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite free <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-module. Since tensor products commute
with direct limits, as does the functor <math id="S6.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, the Proposition
follows from the case already considered.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 6.3</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a noetherian ring <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and a bounded <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-linear functor <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G:\mathbf{Mod}({R})\to\mathbf{Mod}({R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G:\mathbf{Mod}({R})\to\mathbf{Mod}({R})</annotation></semantics></math> that commutes with direct limits.</span></p>
<ol id="S6.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any quasi-finite </span><math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-algebra </span><math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the functor </span><math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{R^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{R^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is
bounded.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any </span><math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{p}\in\spec R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔭</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{p}\in\spec R</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the functor
</span><math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{R_{\mathfrak{p}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{R_{\mathfrak{p}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is bounded.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For (1), by Zariski’s Main Theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx6" title="" class="ltx_ref">EGA</a>, IV.18.12.13]</cite>, the
homomorphism <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\to R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\to R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> factors as <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\to\widetilde{R}\to R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\to\widetilde{R}\to R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\to\widetilde{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\to\widetilde{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite and <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\spec{R^{\prime}}\to\spec\widetilde{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\spec{R^{\prime}}\to\spec\widetilde{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is an open
immersion. Since the functor <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded, the
functor <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\widetilde{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\widetilde{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded. Thus, it suffices to consider the
case where <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\spec R^{\prime}\to\spec R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\spec R^{\prime}\to\spec R</annotation></semantics></math> is an open immersion. For any coherent
<math id="S6.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a coherent <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>
together with an isomorphism of <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>-modules <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\otimes_{R}R^{\prime}\cong M^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\otimes_{R}R^{\prime}\cong M^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the homomorphism <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\to R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\to R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is
flat, Proposition <a href="#S6.Thmthm2" title="Proposition 6.2. ‣ 6.2. Cohomology and base change ‣ 6. Applications ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a> implies that <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(M)\otimes_{R}R^{\prime}\cong G(M\otimes_{R}R^{\prime})\cong G(M^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(M)\otimes_{R}R^{\prime}\cong G(M\otimes_{R}R^{\prime})\cong G(M^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. The functor <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is
bounded, thus the <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S6.SS2.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(M)\otimes_{R}R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(M)\otimes_{R}R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is coherent, giving
the claim.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For (2), fix a coherent <math id="S6.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathfrak{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathfrak{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S6.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, then for
some <math id="S6.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in R-\mathfrak{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔭</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in R-\mathfrak{p}</annotation></semantics></math> there exists an <math id="S6.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S6.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, together
with an <math id="S6.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathfrak{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathfrak{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>-module isomorphism <math id="S6.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\otimes_{R_{f}}R_{\mathfrak{p}}\cong N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\otimes_{R_{f}}R_{\mathfrak{p}}\cong N</annotation></semantics></math>. By Proposition <a href="#S6.Thmthm2" title="Proposition 6.2. ‣ 6.2. Cohomology and base change ‣ 6. Applications ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a>, we have
<math id="S6.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(N)\cong G(L)\otimes_{R_{f}}R_{\mathfrak{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(N)\cong G(L)\otimes_{R_{f}}R_{\mathfrak{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By (1), since <math id="S6.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\to R_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\to R_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is quasi-finite, it follows that <math id="S6.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{R_{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{R_{f}}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded. Thus,
<math id="S6.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(N)</annotation></semantics></math> is a coherent <math id="S6.SS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathfrak{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathfrak{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>-module.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 6.4</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Corollary <a href="#S6.Thmthm3" title="Corollary 6.3. ‣ 6.2. Cohomology and base change ‣ 6. Applications ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.3</span></a>(2) also holds for the henselization and
strict henselization of <math id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathfrak{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathfrak{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a noetherian ring <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and a half-exact, bounded, <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-linear
functor <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\mathbf{Coh}({R})\to\mathbf{Coh}({R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathbf{Coh}({R})\to\mathbf{Coh}({R})</annotation></semantics></math>. A. Ogus and G. Bergman show in
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx27" title="" class="ltx_ref">OB72</a>, Thm. 2.1]</cite> that if for all closed points <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{q}\in\spec R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔮</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{q}\in\spec R</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\kappa(\mathfrak{q}))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\kappa(\mathfrak{q}))=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S6.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is the
zero functor. We have the following amplification.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 6.5</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a noetherian ring <math id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and a bounded, half-exact, <math id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-linear
functor <math id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G:\mathbf{Mod}({R})\to\mathbf{Mod}({R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G:\mathbf{Mod}({R})\to\mathbf{Mod}({R})</annotation></semantics></math> which commutes with direct
limits. Then,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}(G)=\{\mathfrak{q}\in\spec R\,:\,G(\kappa(\mathfrak{q}))=0\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝔮</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.448em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}(G)=\{\mathfrak{q}\in\spec R\,:\,G(\kappa(\mathfrak{q}))=0\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Clearly, if <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{q}\in\mathbb{V}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔮</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{q}\in\mathbb{V}(G)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\kappa(\mathfrak{q}))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\kappa(\mathfrak{q}))=0</annotation></semantics></math>. For the other inclusion, let <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{q}\in\spec R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔮</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{q}\in\spec R</annotation></semantics></math>
satisfy <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\kappa(\mathfrak{q}))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\kappa(\mathfrak{q}))=0</annotation></semantics></math>. By Corollary <a href="#S6.Thmthm3" title="Corollary 6.3. ‣ 6.2. Cohomology and base change ‣ 6. Applications ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.3</span></a>(2),
the functor <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{R_{\mathfrak{q}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝔮</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{R_{\mathfrak{q}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded. Thus, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx27" title="" class="ltx_ref">OB72</a>, Thm. 2.1]</cite> applies, giving <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{R_{\mathfrak{q}}}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝔮</mi></msub></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{R_{\mathfrak{q}}}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and so <math id="S6.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{q}\in\mathbb{V}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔮</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{q}\in\mathbb{V}(G)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">An <math id="S6.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-linear functor <math id="S6.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G:\mathbf{Mod}({R})\to\mathbf{Mod}({R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G:\mathbf{Mod}({R})\to\mathbf{Mod}({R})</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="S6.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">universally bounded</em> if for any
noetherian <math id="S6.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="S6.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the functor <math id="S6.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{R^{\prime}}:\mathbf{Mod}({R^{\prime}})\to\mathbf{Mod}({R^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{R^{\prime}}:\mathbf{Mod}({R^{\prime}})\to\mathbf{Mod}({R^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded. To combine Proposition <a href="#S6.Thmthm1" title="Proposition 6.1. ‣ 6.2. Cohomology and base change ‣ 6. Applications ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a> and
Corollary <a href="#S6.Thmthm5" title="Corollary 6.5. ‣ 6.2. Cohomology and base change ‣ 6. Applications ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.5</span></a>, it is useful to have the following
easily proven Lemma at hand.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.6</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a ring <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and an <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-linear functor <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({A})</annotation></semantics></math>
preserving direct limits. If the functor <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is finitely generated,
then there exists a generator <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I,\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I,\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> a finitely
presented <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-module. In particular, if the ring <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is noetherian,
then the functor <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is universally bounded.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Combining Proposition <a href="#S6.Thmthm1" title="Proposition 6.1. ‣ 6.2. Cohomology and base change ‣ 6. Applications ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>, Corollary
<a href="#S6.Thmthm5" title="Corollary 6.5. ‣ 6.2. Cohomology and base change ‣ 6. Applications ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.5</span></a>, and Lemma <a href="#S6.Thmthm6" title="Lemma 6.6. ‣ 6.2. Cohomology and base change ‣ 6. Applications ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.6</span></a>, we obtain the
vanishing result we desire.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 6.7</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a noetherian ring <math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and an <math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-linear, half-exact functor <math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\mathbf{Mod}({R})\to\mathbf{Mod}({R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathbf{Mod}({R})\to\mathbf{Mod}({R})</annotation></semantics></math> which is finitely generated and preserves
direct limits. If <math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{q}\in\spec R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔮</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{q}\in\spec R</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\kappa(\mathfrak{q}))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\kappa(\mathfrak{q}))=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then there exists <math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in R-\mathfrak{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔮</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in R-\mathfrak{q}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{R_{r}}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{R_{r}}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Corollary <a href="#S6.Thmthm5" title="Corollary 6.5. ‣ 6.2. Cohomology and base change ‣ 6. Applications ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.5</span></a>, <math id="S6.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{q}\in\mathbb{V}(F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔮</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{q}\in\mathbb{V}(F)</annotation></semantics></math>. By
Proposition <a href="#S6.Thmthm1" title="Proposition 6.1. ‣ 6.2. Cohomology and base change ‣ 6. Applications ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>, the set <math id="S6.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}(F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}(F)</annotation></semantics></math> is Zariski open,
thus there exists <math id="S6.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in R-\mathfrak{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔮</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in R-\mathfrak{q}</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S6.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{p}\in\spec R_{r}\subset\mathbb{V}(F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔭</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{p}\in\spec R_{r}\subset\mathbb{V}(F)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S6.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\in\mathbf{Mod}({R_{r}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\mathbf{Mod}({R_{r}})</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="S6.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{p}\in\spec R_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔭</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{p}\in\spec R_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, then by Proposition
<a href="#S6.Thmthm2" title="Proposition 6.2. ‣ 6.2. Cohomology and base change ‣ 6. Applications ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a> it follows that <math id="S6.SS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(N)_{\mathfrak{p}}=F(N_{\mathfrak{p}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔭</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝔭</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(N)_{\mathfrak{p}}=F(N_{\mathfrak{p}})</annotation></semantics></math>. But <math id="S6.SS2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{p}\in\mathbb{V}(F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔭</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{p}\in\mathbb{V}(F)</annotation></semantics></math> and so
<math id="S6.SS2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(N)_{\mathfrak{p}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔭</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(N)_{\mathfrak{p}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S6.SS2.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(N)</annotation></semantics></math> is an <math id="S6.SS2.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>-module, the
result follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">We now combine Corollary <a href="#S6.Thmthm7" title="Corollary 6.7. ‣ 6.2. Cohomology and base change ‣ 6. Applications ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.7</span></a> with the exchange
property proved by A. Ogus and G. Bergman
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx27" title="" class="ltx_ref">OB72</a>, Cor. 5.1]</cite>. Some notation: for a ring <math id="S6.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, a
pair of <math id="S6.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-linear functors <math id="S6.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}:\mathbf{Mod}({A})\to\mathbf{Mod}({A})</annotation></semantics></math> is
<em id="S6.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cohomological</em> if for any exact sequence of <math id="S6.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-modules <math id="S6.SS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\to M^{\prime}\to M\to M^{\prime\prime}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\to M^{\prime}\to M\to M^{\prime\prime}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a functorially induced exact
sequence of <math id="S6.SS2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-modules:</p>
<table id="S6.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S6.Ex11.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="22.16" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-11.069600110696001px" version="1.1" viewBox="27.45 11.07 497.94 22.16" width="497.94"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 27.45302547899803 22.16386089058392) translate(0,3.46) translate(27.45,0)"><g transform="translate(-27.45,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.86" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="46.6"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex11.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{F_{0}(M^{\prime})\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{F_{0}(M^{\prime})\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 27.45302547899803 -0.27673578005007266 L 27.45302547899803 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(60.66,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 27.45302547899803 -0.27673578005007266 L 60.66182581108603 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 60.66182581108603 -0.27673578005007266 L 60.66182581108603 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(60.66,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.09em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="42.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex11.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{F_{0}(M)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{F_{0}(M)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 111.68582716208532 -0.27673578005007266 L 111.68582716208532 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(144.9,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 111.68582716208532 -0.27673578005007266 L 144.89460638058668 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 144.89460638058668 -0.27673578005007266 L 144.89460638058668 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(144.9,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.6em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.86" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="49.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex11.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{F_{0}(M^{\prime\prime})\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{F_{0}(M^{\prime\prime})\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 202.990856938661 -0.27673578005007266 L 202.990856938661 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(236.2,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 202.990856938661 -0.27673578005007266 L 236.1996361571624 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 236.1996361571624 -0.27673578005007266 L 236.1996361571624 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(236.2,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.86" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="46.6"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex11.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{F_{1}(M^{\prime})\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{F_{1}(M^{\prime})\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 291.10568711515845 -0.27673578005007266 L 291.10568711515845 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(324.32,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 291.10568711515845 -0.27673578005007266 L 324.31448744724645 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 324.31448744724645 -0.27673578005007266 L 324.31448744724645 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(324.32,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.09em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="42.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex11.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{F_{1}(M)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{F_{1}(M)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 375.33848879824575 -0.27673578005007266 L 375.33848879824575 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(408.55,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 375.33848879824575 -0.27673578005007266 L 408.54726801674707 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 408.54726801674707 -0.27673578005007266 L 408.54726801674707 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(408.55,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.88em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.86" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="53.64"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex11.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{F_{1}(M^{\prime\prime}).}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{F_{1}(M^{\prime\prime}).}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 6.8</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Property of exchange)<span id="S6.Thmthm8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a noetherian ring <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and a cohomological pair of <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-linear
functors <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}:\mathbf{Mod}({R})\to\mathbf{Mod}({R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}:\mathbf{Mod}({R})\to\mathbf{Mod}({R})</annotation></semantics></math> which are finitely
generated and preserve direct limits. For <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and for any
<math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\in\mathbf{Mod}({R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌𝐨𝐝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\in\mathbf{Mod}({R})</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a natural map:</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}(M):F_{i}(R)\otimes_{R}M\to F_{i}(M)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}(M):F_{i}(R)\otimes_{R}M\to F_{i}(M).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{q}\in\spec R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔮</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{q}\in\spec R</annotation></semantics></math> and suppose that
<math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{0}(\kappa(\mathfrak{q}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{0}(\kappa(\mathfrak{q}))</annotation></semantics></math> is surjective. Then,</span></p>
<ol id="S6.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">there exists </span><math id="S6.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in R-\mathfrak{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔮</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in R-\mathfrak{q}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that for all </span><math id="S6.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\in\mathbf{QCoh}({R_{r}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐𝐂𝐨𝐡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\in\mathbf{QCoh}({R_{r}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the map </span><math id="S6.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{0}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{0}(M)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I2.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is an isomorphism.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The following are equivalent:</span></p>
<ol id="S6.I2.i2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I2.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{1}(\kappa(\mathfrak{q}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{1}(\kappa(\mathfrak{q}))</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is surjective;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the </span><math id="S6.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathfrak{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝔮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathfrak{q}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-module </span><math id="S6.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}(R)_{\mathfrak{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔮</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}(R)_{\mathfrak{q}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is
free.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#S6.Thmthm6" title="Lemma 6.6. ‣ 6.2. Cohomology and base change ‣ 6. Applications ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.6</span></a>, the functors <math id="S6.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are bounded. Now
apply <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx27" title="" class="ltx_ref">OB72</a>, Cor. 5.1]</cite> and Corollary
<a href="#S6.Thmthm7" title="Corollary 6.7. ‣ 6.2. Cohomology and base change ‣ 6. Applications ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.7</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmmainthm1" title="Theorem A. ‣ Introduction ‣ Cohomology and base change for algebraic stacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Throughout we fix a <math id="S6.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-cartesian diagram of noetherian algebraic
stacks:</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
